TITLE:: MIDIKeyboardConfig
SUMMARY:: Contains the configuration for a MIDI keyboard.
CATEGORIES:: Core
RELATED:: Classes/Config

DESCRIPTION::
This class contains the configuration for one MIDI keyboard. LINK::Classes/PipeWire#*connectMidiKeyboards:: uses it to subscribe the keyboard's ALSA sequencer port to the MIDI interface.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new instance of CODE::MIDIKeyboardConfig::.

ARGUMENT:: name
The ALSA sequencer client name, as printed by CODE::aconnect -l::. For example, CODE::"Keystation 61 MK3"::.

ARGUMENT:: port
The port index on that client. CODE::0:: is the first port. On the Keystation 61 MK3, port CODE::0:: is the note output and port CODE::1:: is the transport output.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: name
The ALSA sequencer client name.

METHOD:: port
The port index on that client.

PRIVATE:: init
